# Level 2's spider as the original runs it: as level2-objs.exp (level 1
# won at its 20th frame, the ship kept alive, still and firing, the shop
# skipped), but the spider fought: once the world is held at 2528 the ship
# is put under its right eye (x 224, frame 6650), its left eye (x 64, frame
# 7300), then the middle (x 152, frame 7900). Logged as level2-objs.exp,
# every token taken ($4FF8, for the harness to power its weapons as the
# original's), and every frame the step ($CDA), the back limit ($CEA), the ship's box
# ($39252), the eyes left ($D72), the holes' creatures out ($D74), the
# spider destroyed ($DA6) and the set speed ($CCC).
# Run with --trace fdc.
expect prompt read sector sector=0x1 .*tr=0x0 .*addr=0x6760e
stage level2-jump.ini
stage level2-right.ini
stage level2-left.ini
stage level2-middle.ini
stage level2-spider-start.ini
stage level2-frame.ini
stage weapons-take.ini
stage waves-kill.ini
stage level2-obj.ini
stage level-run-shield.ini
stage level-run-nodeath.ini
stage level-run-nowall.ini
stage level-run-noshop.ini
# Hatari 2.6 loses its breakpoints when a hit adds the 16th (it grows the
# array without copying it): grow it here, outside any hit, then clear it.
debug b pc = $1
debug b pc = $2
debug b pc = $3
debug b pc = $4
debug b pc = $5
debug b pc = $6
debug b pc = $7
debug b pc = $8
debug b pc = $9
debug b pc = $a
debug b pc = $b
debug b pc = $c
debug b pc = $d
debug b pc = $e
debug b pc = $f
debug b pc = $10
debug b pc = $11
debug b pc = $12
debug b pc = $13
debug b pc = $14
debug b pc = $15
debug b pc = $16
debug b all
debug b pc = $7a50 :once :trace :file {run}/level2-spider-start.ini
disk-a {disk2}
sleep 8
fire
sleep 4
fire
expect level1-read read sector sector=0x3 .*tr=0xc .*addr=0x3e
quiet level1-loaded 3
fire
sleep 2
fire
sleep 2
